{
  "$comment": "THE GUARD'S DOOR, WHICH IS THIS MACHINE'S ALONE. The per-call events go to the engine that lives, over HTTP, so no process is started per tool call. The port is derived from this folder's path, so two trees on one machine answer two doors and the cage can name the URL before any engine has started. That number means nothing on another machine, which is why this file is not in version control and .claude/settings.json is. The timeout is short: an engine that has not answered is one that is not there, and the call goes on. PreCompact stays because no session in the record has compacted, and the read set has to be dropped when one does. PostCompact was struck: it never arrived, and a SessionStart whose source is compact is the same moment.",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "http",
            "url": "{{hooks}}",
            "timeout": 3
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "http",
            "url": "{{hooks}}",
            "timeout": 3
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUseFailure": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "http",
            "url": "{{hooks}}",
            "timeout": 3
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "http",
            "url": "{{hooks}}",
            "timeout": 3
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
